{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.QBetaQEqOneShadowGate","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.QBetaQEqOneShadowGate","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.hopf_jones_at_q_one_unfolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.hopf_jones_at_q_one_unfolds","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L120-L124","doc":"**Composition with the exact `J_Hopf(1) = -2` value**: the gate's\nc_3 anchor unfolds to the literal `-2` value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.q_eq_one_shadow_gate_reject_c3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.q_eq_one_shadow_gate_reject_c3","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L107-L118","doc":"**The gate theorem (refute direction, c_3 failure): rejection\nlemma when the c_3 shadow is wrong.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.q_eq_one_shadow_gate_reject_c2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.q_eq_one_shadow_gate_reject_c2","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L91-L105","doc":"**The gate theorem (refute direction, c_2 failure): rejection\nlemma when the c_2 shadow is wrong.**\n\nIf a candidate predicts `c2 1 = a` with `a ≠ -1`, then the class\ncannot be instantiated for `(c2, c3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.qbeta_q_eq_one_shadow_anchors","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.qbeta_q_eq_one_shadow_anchors","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L72-L89","doc":"**The gate theorem (forward direction): under the class, the\ncandidate's q=1 shadows match the canonical anchors.**\n\nRoutine restatement of the class fields; the value of formalising\nis composition with downstream checks (cross-anchor swing, radius\nof convergence, bar-evenness).\n\n**Assumed, not derived here.** \"Routine restatement\" is exact: the body\nis `⟨hC.c2_at_one_eq_neg_one, hC.c3_at_one_eq_jones_hopf⟩`, both\nconjuncts projected verbatim from `QOneShadowGateClass`. The anchors are\nhypotheses on `c2`/`c3`, which are arbitrary functions here, so the\nstatement is genuinely conditional and may not be strengthened to a\nglobal `axiom`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate","label":"prop:q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.c3_at_one_eq_jones_hopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.c3_at_one_eq_jones_hopf","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The c_3 classical-limit shadow equals the Hopf-Jones value `-2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.c2_at_one_eq_neg_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.c2_at_one_eq_neg_one","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The c_2 classical-limit shadow equals the PR #1786 anchor `-1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.QOneShadowGateClass","kind":"class","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L51-L70","doc":"**q = 1 classical-limit shadow gate class (§3b-cond, PARAMETRIC).**\n\nParametric over the candidate coefficient functions `c2 c3 : ℝ → ℝ`\n(per Gemini high-priority review on PR #1890): this allows any\nfuture kernel candidate to be checked by instantiating the class\nwith its own coefficient pair, rather than locking the class to a\nsingle global axiom. This is essential for the Track C unified\ntypeclass composition.\n\nAxiomatises both canonical integer shadows in a single class:\n`c2 1 = -1` (PR #1786 Taylor-exact) and `c3 1 = -2 = J_Hopf(1)`\n(registry §3 anchor). A candidate must satisfy BOTH to instantiate\nthe class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.hopfJonesAtQOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.QOneShadowGate.hopfJonesAtQOne","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/q-beta-q-eq-one-shadow-gate.lean#L44-L49","doc":"**The canonical Hopf-Jones classical value.**\n\n`J_Hopf(q = 1) = -2` is the categorical anchor for the inter-block\nN=3 correction; recorded as a definitional constant. ","signatureChunk":0}]}